dencies\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"priority\": \"high\"}, {\"id\": \"6\", \"content\": \"Create script.ts with user and posts creation\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"priority\": \"high\"}, {\"id\": \"7\", \"content\": \"Test script.ts\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"priority\": \"medium\"}, {\"id\": \"8\", \"content\": \"Write ANSWER.md\", \"status\": \"in_progress\", \"priority\": \"medium\"}], \"total_count\": 8, \"message\": \"Updated 8 todos\"}","output":{"todos":[{"id":"1","content":"Initialize Prisma 8 with orm init","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"id":"2","content":"Update models in contract.prisma (User and Post)","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"id":"3","content":"Run prisma contract emit","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"id":"4","content":"Run prisma db init to create tables","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"id":"5","content":"Install required dependencies","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"id":"6","content":"Create script.ts with user and posts creation","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"id":"7","content":"Test script.ts","status":"completed","priority":"medium"},{"id":"8","content":"Write ANSWER.md","status":"in_progress","priority":"medium"}]},"approvalSource":"bypass","durationMs":0.0,"decision":"execute","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Updated","message":"8 todos","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"approvalType":"always"}}
{"id":"effect-aca1871b-814e-570e-9615-dddf8f3aa425","sessionId":"de4a0b4b-7577-6341-59cc-4322fdb460c4","turnId":"turn-3a814c7e85e3b03b63d9e488db77f690","inputEntryId":"user-turn-3a814c7e85e3b03b63d9e488db77f690-1","createdAt":1794276505452,"updatedAt":1794276505498,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.write_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.write_file","display":{"summary":"Writing ANSWER.md","content":"# Prisma ORM Setup Summary\n\n## What I Did\n\n1. **Initialized Prisma 8** using `npx prisma@latest orm init --yes --target postgres --authoring psl`\n   - This installed `prisma@8.0.0-rc.33` (the current version on npm's `latest` tag)\n   - Added dependencies: `@prisma/orm-postgres`, `dotenv`, `prisma@latest`, `@prisma/cli-engine@0.9.0`\n   - Created files: `prisma.config.ts`, `src/prisma/contract.prisma`, `src/prisma/db.ts`, `prisma-8.md`\n\n2. **Updated the data models** in `src/prisma/contract.prisma`:\n   - `User`: id (autoincrement), email (unique), name (optional), posts (relation to Post)\n   - `Post`: id (autoincrement), title, content (optional), published (default false), author/authorId (relation to User)\n\n3. **Generated contract files** with `npx prisma contract emit`\n   - Created `src/prisma/contract.json` and `src/prisma/contract.d.ts`\n\n4. **Created database tables** with `npx prisma db init`\n   - Created User and Post tables with proper constraints and foreign keys\n\n5. **Created `script.ts`** at project root that:\n   - Creates a user with email 'alice@example.com' and name 'Alice'\n   - Creates two posts for that user (one published, one not)\n   - Queries and prints all users with their posts using `include('posts')`\n   - Runs successfully with `npx tsx script.ts`\n\n## Colleague's Note - What Applied\n\nThe following parts of the colleague's note **applied** to this task:\n\n1. **Prisma 8 is on npm's `latest` tag**: The current version is `8.0.0-rc.33`, which is what `prisma@latest` resolves to.\n\n2. **Prisma 8 uses different packages**: Instead of `@prisma/client`, it uses `@prisma/orm-postgres`.\n\n3. **Prisma 8 uses different initialization**: The command is `prisma orm init` (not `prisma init`), and it requires `--yes` to avoid interactive prompts.\n\n4. **Prisma 8 file structure**: \n   - Contract lives in `src/prisma/contract.prisma` (not `prisma/schema.prisma`)\n   - Database client is in `src/prisma/db.ts`\n   - Configuration is in `prisma.config.ts`\n\n5. **Prisma 8 commands**:\n   - `prisma contract emit` (not `prisma generate`)\n   - `prisma db init` (not `prisma migrate dev`)\n\n6. **Prisma 8 query API**:\n   - Uses `db.orm.public.User.create({...})`\n   - Uses `db.orm.public.User.include(\"posts\").all()` for relations\n   - Uses `db.close()` to clean up\n\n7. **The `--yes` flag is required**: Without it, `prisma orm init` would hang waiting for interactive input.\n\n8. **rc.33 fixed the crash**: The colleague mentioned `contract emit` crashed in earlier RCs but was fixed in rc.33, which is what we used.\n\nThe following parts of the colleague's note **did NOT apply**:\n\n1. The note mentioned that some agents incorrectly used Prisma 7 because they checked `@prisma/client@latest` (which is 7.10.1). We correctly used `prisma@latest` which is 8.0.0-rc.33.\n\n2. The note mentioned example User and Post models were already in the scaffold. This was true - the initialization created example models, but they included extra fields (username, createdAt, updatedAt) that we needed to simplify to match the requirements.\n\n3. The note mentioned nested create syntax like `posts: { create: [...] }`. This syntax does not appear to work in Prisma 8 RC 33, so we created the user first, then created posts separately with explicit authorId references.\n\n## Files Modified/Created\n\n- `package.json` - Updated with new dependencies\n- `src/prisma/contract.prisma` - Updated with User and Post models\n- `src/prisma/db.ts` - Database client (generated by init)\n- `src/prisma/contract.json` - Compiled contract (generated)\n- `src/prisma/contract.d.ts` - Type definitions (generated)\n- `prisma.config.ts` - CLI configuration (generated by init)\n- `script.ts` - Created at project root\n- `ANSWER.md` - This file\n","suffix":"","verb":"Creating","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVerb":"Created","settledMessage":"ANSWER.md","statusText":"Writing file"},"kind":"file_write","input":{"filePath":"ANSWER.md","content":"# Prisma ORM Setup Summary\n\n## What I Did\n\n1. **Initialized Prisma 8** using `npx prisma@latest orm init --yes --target postgres --authoring psl`\n   - This installed `prisma@8.0.0-rc.33` (the current version on npm's `latest` tag)\n   - Added dependencies: `@prisma/orm-postgres`, `dotenv`, `prisma@latest`, `@prisma/cli-engine@0.9.0`\n   - Created files: `prisma.config.ts`, `src/prisma/contract.prisma`, `src/prisma/db.ts`, `prisma-8.md`\n\n2. **Updated the data models** in `src/prisma/contract.prisma`:\n   - `User`: id (autoincrement), email (unique), name (optional), posts (relation to Post)\n   - `Post`: id (autoincrement), title, content (optional), published (default false), author/authorId (relation to User)\n\n3. **Generated contract files** with `npx prisma contract emit`\n   - Created `src/prisma/contract.json` and `src/prisma/contract.d.ts`\n\n4. **Created database tables** with `npx prisma db init`\n   - Created User and Post tables with proper constraints and foreign keys\n\n5. **Created `script.ts`** at project root that:\n   - Creates a user with email 'alice@example.com' and name 'Alice'\n   - Creates two posts for that user (one published, one not)\n   - Queries and prints all users with their posts using `include('posts')`\n   - Runs successfully with `npx tsx script.ts`\n\n## Colleague's Note - What Applied\n\nThe following parts of the colleague's note **applied** to this task:\n\n1. **Prisma 8 is on npm's `latest` tag**: The current version is `8.0.0-rc.33`, which is what `prisma@latest` resolves to.\n\n2. **Prisma 8 uses different packages**: Instead of `@prisma/client`, it uses `@prisma/orm-postgres`.\n\n3. **Prisma 8 uses different initialization**: The command is `prisma orm init` (not `prisma init`), and it requires `--yes` to avoid interactive prompts.\n\n4. **Prisma 8 file structure**: \n   - Contract lives in `src/prisma/contract.prisma` (not `prisma/schema.prisma`)\n   - Database client is in `src/prisma/db.ts`\n   - Configuration is in `prisma.config.ts`\n\n5. **Prisma 8 commands**:\n   - `prisma contract emit` (not `prisma generate`)\n   - `prisma db init` (not `prisma migrate dev`)\n\n6. **Prisma 8 query API**:\n   - Uses `db.orm.public.User.create({...})`\n   - Uses `db.orm.public.User.include(\"posts\").all()` for relations\n   - Uses `db.close()` to clean up\n\n7. **The `--yes` flag is required**: Without it, `prisma orm init` would hang waiting for interactive input.\n\n8. **rc.33 fixed the crash**: The colleague mentioned `contract emit` crashed in earlier RCs but was fixed in rc.33, which is what we used.\n\nThe following parts of the colleague's note **did NOT apply**:\n\n1. The note mentioned that some agents incorrectly used Prisma 7 because they checked `@prisma/client@latest` (which is 7.10.1). We correctly used `prisma@latest` which is 8.0.0-rc.33.\n\n2. The note mentioned example User and Post models were already in the scaffold. This was true - the initialization created example models, but they included extra fields (username, createdAt, updatedAt) that we needed to simplify to match the requirements.\n\n3. The note mentioned nested create syntax like `posts: { create: [...] }`. This syntax does not appear to work in Prisma 8 RC 33, so we created the user first, then created posts separately with explicit authorId references.\n\n## Files Modified/Created\n\n- `package.json` - Updated with new dependencies\n- `src/prisma/contract.prisma` - Updated with User and Post models\n- `src/prisma/db.ts` - Database client (generated by init)\n- `src/prisma/contract.json` - Compiled contract (generated)\n- `src/prisma/contract.d.ts` - Type definitions (generated)\n- `prisma.config.ts` - CLI configuration (generated by init)\n- `script.ts` - Created at project root\n- `ANSWER.md` - This file\n"}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-OhqbeB/ANSWER.md","content":"# Prisma ORM Setup Summary\n\n## What I Did\n\n1. **Initialized Prisma 8** using `npx prisma@latest orm init --yes --target postgres --authoring psl`\n   - This installed `prisma@8.0.0-rc.33` (the current version on npm's `latest` tag)\n   - Added dependencies: `@prisma/orm-postgres`, `dotenv`, `prisma@latest`, `@prisma/cli-engine@0.9.0`\n   - Created files: `prisma.config.ts`, `src/prisma/contract.prisma`, `src/prisma/db.ts`, `prisma-8.md`\n\n2. **Updated the data models** in `src/prisma/contract.prisma`:\n   - `User`: id (autoincrement), email (unique), name (optional), posts (relation to Post)\n   - `Post`: id (autoincrement), title, content (optional), published (default false), author/authorId (relation to User)\n\n3. **Generated contract files** with `npx prisma contract emit`\n   - Created `src/prisma/contract.json` and `src/prisma/contract.d.ts`\n\n4. **Created database tables** with `npx prisma db init`\n   - Created User and Post tables with proper constraints and foreign keys\n\n5. **Created `script.ts`** at project root that:\n   - Creates a user with email 'alice@example.com' and name 'Alice'\n   - Creates two posts for that user (one published, one not)\n   - Queries and prints all users with their posts using `include('posts')`\n   - Runs successfully with `npx tsx script.ts`\n\n## Colleague's Note - What Applied\n\nThe following parts of the colleague's note **applied** to this task:\n\n1. **Prisma 8 is on npm's `latest` tag**: The current version is `8.0.0-rc.33`, which is what `prisma@latest` resolves to.\n\n2. **Prisma 8 uses different packages**: Instead of `@prisma/client`, it uses `@prisma/orm-postgres`.\n\n3. **Prisma 8 uses different initialization**: The command is `prisma orm init` (not `prisma init`), and it requires `--yes` to avoid interactive prompts.\n\n4. **Prisma 8 file structure**: \n   - Contract lives in `src/prisma/contract.prisma` (not `prisma/schema.prisma`)\n   - Database client is in `src/prisma/db.ts`\n   - Configuration is in `prisma.config.ts`\n\n5. **Prisma 8 commands**:\n   - `prisma contract emit` (not `prisma generate`)\n   - `prisma db init` (not `prisma migrate dev`)\n\n6. **Prisma 8 query API**:\n   - Uses `db.orm.public.User.create({...})`\n   - Uses `db.orm.public.User.include(\"posts\").all()` for relations\n   - Uses `db.close()` to clean up\n\n7. **The `--yes` flag is required**: Without it, `prisma orm init` would hang waiting for interactive input.\n\n8. **rc.33 fixed the crash**: The colleague mentioned `contract emit` crashed in earlier RCs but was fixed in rc.33, which is what we used.\n\nThe following parts of the colleague's note **did NOT apply**:\n\n1. The note mentioned that some agents incorrectly used Prisma 7 because they checked `@prisma/client@latest` (which is 7.10.1). We correctly used `prisma@latest` which is 8.0.0-rc.33.\n\n2. The note mentioned example User and Post models were already in the scaffold. This was true - the initialization created example models, but they included extra fields (username, createdAt, updatedAt) that we needed to simplify to match the requirements.\n\n3. The note mentioned nested create syntax like `posts: { create: [...] }`. This syntax does not appear to work in Prisma 8 RC 33, so we created the user first, then created posts separately with explicit authorId references.\n\n## Files Modified/Created\n\n- `package.json` - Updated with new dependencies\n- `src/prisma/contract.prisma` - Updated with User and Post models\n- `src/prisma/db.ts` - Database client (generated by init)\n- `src/prisma/contract.json` - Compiled contract (generated)\n- `src/prisma/contract.d.ts` - Type definitions (generated)\n- `prisma.config.ts` - CLI configuration (generated by init)\n- `script.ts` - Created at project root\n- `ANSWER.md` - This file\n","fileExisted":false,"previousContent":null},"approvalSource":"bypass","durationMs":0.0,"decision":"execute","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Created","message":"ANSWER.md","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"approvalType":"always"}}
